{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1406116-in-need-of-condition-assitance","id":1406116,"title":"In need of Condition assitance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-03T08:26:17-07:00","id":1406116,"title":"In need of Condition assitance","content":"So one of my players want to play an achantus who is cursed with having severely bad luck. So they can go from extremely bad luck to super good luck when they use their arcanums. Are there any conditions that covers bad luck of that magnitude? Or any ideas for custom ones that can halp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T10:04:07-07:00","id":1406123,"title":"","content":"You could take Zone of Extremity from 1ed and make it affect spellcasting only.<br /> <br /> It could also have the side effect of amplifying any yantra that makes them take real risk without magical assistance. Like going into a gunfight with only one bullet gives a +2, +3 if they don't know which barrel has the gun (a reverse Russian roulette). Another example is making a bet where they could lose Resources for a month and not influencing the outcome.<br /> <br /> Arcane beats could be given from winning such gambles, the resolution based on a story milestone they need to figure out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 08-03-2020, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T10:35:00-07:00","id":1406124,"title":"","content":"A few quick ways you could model that:<br /> - X times per session, a mundane action roll becomes a chance die<br /> - Downgrade every outcome one degree: failures become dramatic failures, successes become basic failures, exceptional successes become basic successes<br /> - Every roll incurs an additional cost, drawback, or complication, regardless of its primary outcome (see \u201cThreats\u201d in Genesys) <br /> - Use the \u201cHex\u201d rules (Mage 2E, 134), such as imposing a dice penalty on all mundane actions<br /> - Miracle Fate (Mage 2E, 140) decreases the number of successes rolled by 1, causing a dramatic failure if less than 0, on a number of rolls equal to potency.<br /> - For something more under the players control, you can tweak the rules (only for them) for the voluntary dramatic failure: require them to voluntarily dramatically fail (before rolling) like 3 times in a scene before they can earn a Beat.<br /> - The Curse Haunt (Geist 2E) imposes a -2 to rolls a number of times (equal to plasm spent) or breaks equipment, causes tilts, starts fires, deals damage, or makes them ignored by everyone<br /> - Changing Fortunes (CtL 2E) imposes a -2 or raises the exceptional success threshold by 1, for each success on the activation.<br /> - Spinning Wheel (CtL 2E) states a specific even the character will experience, and grants +5 to anything which hurries that event or -5 to everything which obstructs it.<br /> <br /> I would personally favor turning this curse into a story book, by putting an unknown signature nimbus on the character, and/or use the curse to drive the character towards some specific outcome. An Archmage, Supernal being, True Fae, powerful spirit, or an Aeon could all levy a such a curse with a very obscured agenda and too powerful to remove - but most such affects don\u2019t apply to spell casting rolls by default, especially not if the curse was made before they Awakened. <br /> <br /> Hope something in there helps you~","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T10:41:58-07:00","id":1406125,"title":"","content":"Slap a reverse Destiny on them? They have a pool of Disaster each Chapter, at any time the ST may turn a mundane action into a chance die roll a number of times equal to their Disaster pool. This also comes with a Quest that will lift the curse...eventually, when taking actions that would fulfill the requirements of the Quest they may gain 5 dice from a WP expenditure instead of 3. If the roll fails anyway they don\u2019t lose the WP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}